{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Ephraim, he mixes</b> — like בלול, mixed. And the meaning: they seek help from the nations, this one because of that one, and this is: \"Egypt they call, Assyria they go\" (Hosea 7:11); therefore he mixes among the peoples like בלול. And Egypt are the ones calling." "<b>A cake unturned</b> — then it is burnt when it is not turned. And the meaning: because of their counsel and because their passion and heart are like an oven (Hosea 7:6), the counsel is likened to a cake."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The phrase לזה מפני זה is rendered literally; the syntax is compressed and the referents are implied."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:30.481022925Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}